	"notes": [
		{
			"id": "nTgdtgsyJrYat7bhW",
			"text": "Typical Stats from the package record: ST 3, DX 13, IQ 2, HT 10, HP 3, WILL 8, PER 9, FP 10, SPEED 5.75, MOVE 5, DODGE 8, DR 0. GCS derives its own values by applying the ancestry; where the two differ, the package's Typical Stats are what the Dungeons on Automatic encounter tables use."
		},
		{
			"id": "nuqCB89QBvy9ZU1Ki",
			"text": "Encounter rating: CER 7 (offense 16, protection -9), threat tier minor, appearing 1."
		},
		{
			"id": "nP-Qu9HlXlN8SF65O",
			"text": "Swarming Bites: No attack roll and no active defense. Swarming Bites: 1d-4 impaling, Reach C. No attack roll and no defence. Roll HT against the combined venom of several hundred bites or take fever and a shaking hand for the rest of the day."
		},
		{
			"id": "nzkWgQGFjzSR-2W9k",
			"text": "GCS ancestry draft: gcs/spider-swarm.gct"
		},
		{
			"id": "nMqnrcnQEcFe2Gqxm",
			"text": "Independent build total: -19 points of racial traits plus 0 points of racial skills."
		},
		{
			"id": "n2OilW6wXBLTkOwm3",
			"text": "Answers the SRD heading(s): Spider Swarm (SRD 3.5). Only the creature identity is taken from the SRD; the GURPS statistics, ratings and prose are this project's own work and reproduce no SRD text."
		},
		{
			"id": "nQwYP8aNfn7xA3Btd",
			"text": "Typical Stats, damage and ratings are derived from the racial template, not authored beside it, so the sheet and the stat block cannot disagree."
		},
		{
			"id": "nmNIUXSTafejbeEVJ",
			"text": "Body mass used to scale this build: 2 kg. ST, Size Modifier and DR are checked against it; see the gurps-animal-sanity-check skill for the bands."
		},
		{
			"id": "ns7CLHaeUvLhELM4L",
			"text": "Movement: ground Move 5 (primary). The published Move is the primary medium's cruising Move; sprint figures are stated here and not folded into it."
		},
		{
			"id": "nVb96FEwXbZr-4BMD",
			"text": "Treasure and grappling are not authored for this batch and ship as explicit nulls; `lair` carries a short habitat note, because where a wandering animal dens is an encounter fact rather than a loot one."
		},
		{
			"id": "n2lEGZGatBO4Z0-Pz",
			"text": "One hex of swarm, which is where the Size Modifier comes from."
		},
		{
			"id": "nOPnMZpTuaglx0VLG",
